Menu="DiskUsage:2"
Title="Settings"
Tag="gear"
---
<?php
require_once '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/duc/include/common.php';
$cfg = duc_config();
$paths = implode("\n", duc_index_paths($cfg));
$excludes = implode("\n", duc_exclude_patterns($cfg));
?>
<script>
function ducPrepare(form) {
  // Settings are stored as single-line ini values; keep one entry per line in the UI.
  form.INDEX_PATHS.value = form.INDEX_PATHS_UI.value.split(/\n/).map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean).join(',');
  form.EXCLUDE.value = form.EXCLUDE_UI.value.split(/\n/).map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean).join(',');
  form.INDEX_PATHS_UI.disabled = true;
  form.EXCLUDE_UI.disabled = true;
}
function ducSchedule(form) {
  var s = form.SCHEDULE.value;
  $('#duc-hour').toggle(s === 'daily' || s === 'weekly' || s === 'monthly');
  $('#duc-custom').toggle(s === 'custom');
}
function ducHistory(form) {
  $('#duc-history-opts').toggle(form.HISTORY.value === 'yes');
}
$(function() { ducSchedule(document.duc_settings); ducHistory(document.duc_settings); });
</script>

<form markdown="1" name="duc_settings" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame" onsubmit="ducPrepare(this)">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="duc/duc.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/duc/scripts/apply-settings">
<input type="hidden" name="INDEX_PATHS" value="">
<input type="hidden" name="EXCLUDE" value="">

_(Paths to index)_:
: <textarea name="INDEX_PATHS_UI" rows="4" spellcheck="false" style="width:400px"><?=htmlspecialchars($paths)?></textarea>

> One path per line. Indexing `/mnt/user` shows usage by share. Index `/mnt/disk1`, `/mnt/cache` etc. instead
> (or as well) to see usage per disk or pool; scanning disks directly is faster than going through `/mnt/user`.
> Indexing reads directory metadata on every disk involved, so spun-down disks will spin up during a run.

_(Exclude patterns)_:
: <textarea name="EXCLUDE_UI" rows="3" spellcheck="false" style="width:400px" placeholder="*.tmp"><?=htmlspecialchars($excludes)?></textarea>

> One shell glob pattern per line. Matching files and folders are left out of the index.

_(Index database)_:
: <input type="text" name="DB_PATH" style="width:400px" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['DB_PATH'])?>">

> Where the index is stored. The default lives in `appdata` so it survives a reboot. Avoid the USB flash
> drive (`/boot`) because the database is rewritten on every run. The index of a large array can be a few hundred MB.

_(Schedule)_:
: <select name="SCHEDULE" onchange="ducSchedule(this.form)">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SCHEDULE'], 'disabled', _('Disabled (manual only)'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SCHEDULE'], 'hourly', _('Hourly'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SCHEDULE'], 'daily', _('Daily'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SCHEDULE'], 'weekly', _('Weekly'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SCHEDULE'], 'monthly', _('Monthly'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SCHEDULE'], 'custom', _('Custom'))?>
  </select>

<div markdown="1" id="duc-hour">
_(Time of day)_:
: <select name="HOUR">
  <?php for ($h = 0; $h < 24; $h++) echo mk_option($cfg['HOUR'], (string)$h, sprintf('%02d:00', $h)); ?>
  </select>
</div>

<div markdown="1" id="duc-custom">
_(Custom cron schedule)_:
: <input type="text" name="CUSTOM_CRON" style="width:200px" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['CUSTOM_CRON'])?>">

> Five cron fields: minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week, e.g. `30 2 * * 1-5`.
</div>

_(Run at low priority)_:
: <select name="LOW_PRIORITY">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['LOW_PRIORITY'], 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['LOW_PRIORITY'], 'no', _('No'))?>
  </select>

> Runs the indexer with `nice` and idle I/O priority so it stays out of the way of other work.

_(Stay on one file system)_:
: <select name="ONE_FS">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['ONE_FS'], 'no', _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['ONE_FS'], 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

> Skip folders that are on a different file system, such as mounts inside a share.

_(Count hard links once)_:
: <select name="HARD_LINKS">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HARD_LINKS'], 'no', _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HARD_LINKS'], 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

> Useful when you use hard links, for example with the *arr apps. This uses more memory while indexing.

_(Keep size history)_:
: <select name="HISTORY" onchange="ducHistory(this.form)">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY'], 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY'], 'no', _('No'))?>
  </select>

> After each index run the folder sizes are added to a small history file next to the index
> (`<?=htmlspecialchars(duc_history_file($cfg))?>`). The Disk Usage page then shows how a folder grew over time
> and the change per subfolder. Nothing extra is scanned; the sizes come from the new index.

<div markdown="1" id="duc-history-opts">
_(History depth)_:
: <select name="HISTORY_DEPTH">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY_DEPTH'], '1', _('Top level only'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY_DEPTH'], '2', _('Two levels'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY_DEPTH'], '3', _('Three levels'))?>
  </select>

> With `/mnt/user` indexed, the top level is the shares. Deeper folders are only recorded from 1 GB.

_(Keep history for)_:
: <select name="HISTORY_DAYS">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY_DAYS'], '365', _('1 year'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY_DAYS'], '730', _('2 years'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY_DAYS'], '1825', _('5 years'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['HISTORY_DAYS'], '0', _('Forever'))?>
  </select>
</div>

_(Notifications)_:
: <select name="NOTIFY">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY'], 'none', _('None'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY'], 'error', _('Errors only'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['NOTIFY'], 'all', _('Errors and completed runs'))?>
  </select>

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" value="_(Apply)_"><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">

</form>

> The `duc` command is also available from the Unraid terminal. To browse in the terminal, run
> `duc ui -d <?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['DB_PATH'])?> /mnt/user`.
